Z||000000||Luperman||01-09-2000||03:30 AM||||1st my 86 SE V-6 (auto) seems to stumble while travling between 45-70 MPH with the gas pedal steady(it's like someone is turning on and off my fuel pump but it is irregular), push on the gas stumble goes away, when at 70 and above smooth sailing power to spare.<BR> I have tuned it up changed the plugs wires had a new distributor installed cap and rotor.<P>2nd question is when I first start it up it idles great put in and out of gear engine stays running , after you drive for a little while you come to a stop and put it in park the engine dies but has no problem starting again but you have to keep your foot on the gas so it won't die once you have it in fwd or rev for 30 seconds it will usally stay running(this problem is intermittant also .<BR>any help would be appreciated thanks  <p>[This message has been edited by Luperman (edited 01-09-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||ka4nkf||01-09-2000||07:39 PM||||On your first question, Mine had a hesitation when running around 30 or 40 i checked everything i could find and came up with nothing. Then one day my check engine light came on and i got the code 32 from the ecm. So i unpluged the egr valve and ran it and it ran like a new engine. The egr contrl solenoid is $98.00 dollors, so i am running it without egr, You might unpluge your egr valve and try it. Dont hurt to try. On your second question i do not have an answer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||01-10-2000||02:11 AM||||I have the same car! 86 SE Auto. Nice to drive.<P>The EGR will slam closed on a large increase in throttle position. It could be the EGR is leaking or the control solenoid is leaking and it's metering more exhaust than needed. When you press the throttle (or just change positions), the solenoid closes and even if it is leaking, the "leak" is little EGR flow and it improves.<P>If you do disconnect it or block the passage, listen for pinging at high throttle position/low engine RPM (lugging). It will ping without the EGR. <P>Just be careful and back out of the throttle if you hear it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||01-10-2000||09:07 AM||||It could be your lock up torque converter cutting in and out causing the hunting feeling.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Luperman||01-12-2000||11:14 PM||||I thought you were'nt supposed to block off the egr valve. ||||reg||5
Z||000005||theogre||01-13-2000||07:05 PM||||I don't think the TC lockup would cause these problems. That is easy to see on the tac. the dif from locked to unlocked is about 200rpm.<P>sounds more like ignition timing or a vac leak.||||reg||1
